	(lib_symbols)
	(text_box "DESIGN NOTES - M1421\n\nADSBee m1421 (lib ADSB_Test:PantsForBirds_ADSBee_m1421, official PantsForBirds kicad-libs, MIT). VCC 1.8-3.3 V -> 3V3_M1421 (switched, PM3 ch2), ~19 mA.\nGND pads 6,18,23,25,27,34,36 + both MP thermal pads: FILLED+CAPPED vias (also under GND pads beside RF pins). Paste on all exposed pads. Respect footprint top-copper keepouts.\nConsole UART 1 Mbaud: SUTX(21) -> P4 UART3 RX + Dev RP2040 RX. SURX(20) <- 74LVC1G157 mux (default P4 TX; RP2040 TX when its select is high).\nSYNC(28) is an INPUT (host-driven): high at reset = ROM UART bootloader, high at runtime = sleep + LR2021 bus release. SYNC = P4_SYNC OR DEV_SYNC (74LVC1G32, target powered; DEV_SYNC pulled low). 100k pull-down. LA CH6.\n~SRST(17): open-drain wired-AND from TCA6408A bit7, RP2040 (74LVC1G07 Ioff) and JTAG header pin 10.\nJTAG JMSC(8) JCKC(9) JTDO(10) JTDI(11) -> 2x5 1.27 mm Cortex header (as carrier) for Segger J-Link, target CC1314R10, JTAG 4 MHz.\nSD26(15) 1090 activity -> red LED + LA CH7. SD27(16) UAT activity -> green LED + LA CH11. SD23-25: test pads.\nLR2021 lines (2,3,5,7,29-33) and LRFH(35): test pads only.\nRF: SRF(24, 978) + LRFL(26, 1090) -> SCN-2-11+ combiner (100R across ports) -> ESD7351 -> edge SMA on the RF edge (opposite the digital connectors). Copy carrier CPW geometry. Optional two-piece RF can (frame fitted, lid removable) over m1421 + combiner; clear 2.7 mm module height."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
